<title>UK: Lex up after results.</title>
<headline>Lex up after results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK vehicle retailer Lex Service Plc climbed to a three-month high after the group posted a 22 percent rise in its 1996 profits and said it was encouraged by its performance so far this year, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were up 12p to 343-1/2p by 1336 GMT on turnover of 1.8 million shares.</p>
<p>Earlier, the company said its pre-tax, pre-exceptional profits rose to 51.4 million.</p>
<p>The shares had been rising earlier this week in advance of the report. Also, analysts at Merrill Lynch rated the the stock a &quot;buy&quot; on Monday.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
